Well, I don't know if these are known or not, or if they're bugs at
all, but I encountered them in my whole-weekend playing spree (which
I'm still recovering from):

-a doppelganger, when turned into a seregent, is still white, not red!
I was confused when the game kept telling me that "the seregent swings
his flail!" when the only @ next to me was white-colored. Perhaps it's
a limited-circumstance thing? Probably testable in wiz-mode with
monster-poly-control and ^G. (Yes, it was a doppelganger... or at least
it was an albino seregent carrying a doppelganger corpse!)

-after phasing as a xorn and returning to human form (on solid ground),
the game says "you are in a pit" and you must crawl out. After you do,
you find that there is no pit in the ground! (this has already been
fixed, it seems)

-after taming a sleeping jabberwock (this took a long time, as I was
playing a rogue), saddling it, and riding it around, applying a
stethoscope > still shows that it's asleep, and the jabberwock won't
move of its own accord. After it was attacked, it finally managed to
wake up. Sleepwalking jabberwocks? You find something new every day!



